+**Numbered Steps:**
+1. Initialize ray origin and direction for each pixel [G].
+2. For each pass $i$ from $1$ to $P$:
+   a. Set the rendering resolution to $r_i \times \text{Final Resolution}$ [G].
+   b. Allocate $n_i = \lfloor f_i \times N_{\text{total}} \rfloor$ iterations for sphere tracing for each active ray [S1, unofficial].
+   c. Perform sphere tracing for $n_i$ steps, updating the ray position $p \leftarrow p + \text{step\_size}(p)$ [G].
+   d. If a surface is hit (distance $< \epsilon$), mark the pixel as hit and skip remaining passes for that ray [G].
+3. Composite the results from the final pass (or the pass where the hit occurred) into the final image buffer [G].
+
+**Formulas:**
+*   Iterations per pass: $n_i = \lfloor f_i \times N_{\text{total}} \rfloor$
+*   Resolution per pass: $\text{Res}_i = r_i \times \text{Res}_{\text{final}}$
+*   Step update: $p_{k+1} = p_k + \text{step\_size}(p_k)$, where $\text{step\_size}$ follows the chosen sphere tracing variant (e.g., $r - 1 + \omega \cdot r'$ for enhanced sphere tracing) [S1, unofficial].
 
